/*
Given a target integer T and an integer array A sorted in ascending order, find the index i in A such that A[i] is closest to T.

Assumptions

There can be duplicate elements in the array, and we can return any of the indices with same value.
Examples

A = {1, 2, 3}, T = 2, return 1
A = {1, 4, 6}, T = 3, return 1
A = {1, 4, 6}, T = 5, return 1 or 2
A = {1, 3, 3, 4}, T = 2, return 0 or 1 or 2
Corner Cases

What if A is null or A is of zero length? We should return -1 in this case
*/

public int ClosestElementBinarySearch(int[] array, target){
    int left = 0;
    int right = array.length - 1;

    int largerMin = 0;
    int smallerMax = 0;
    
    while(left <= right){
        int mid = left + (right - left)/2;
        if(array[mid] == target){
            return mid;
        }
        else if(array[mid] > target){
            largerMin = mid;
            right = mid - 1;
        }
        else if(array[mid] < target){
            smallerMax = mid - 1;
            left = mid + 1;
        }
    }

    if(Math.abs(smallerMax - target) >= Math.abs(largerMin - target)){
        return largerMin;
    }
    else{
        return smallerMax;
    }
}

/*
思路基于BS母题2:

很简单，首先我们知道距离最近的肯定是这个target本身，因此我们就把这个题转换成了一个BS题
但是tricky的点在于target有可能不在array中，这一点的限制就把这个题目转换成了向左向右找first occurrence的题目
找first occurrence的关键点在于利用一个变量暂存
找到之后，我们算两边的first occurrence到target的绝对值再进行比较就可以得到更近的那个元素
返回index即可
*/